      ],
      "investment_income": [
        "Interest on Reserves"
      ],
      "note": "For a 501(c)(6) business league, membership dues and qualified sponsorship payments are reported as contributions (Form 990 Part VIII line 1), not program service revenue. Convention and trade show income, registrations, training and certification fees are program service revenue (line 2). Interest is investment income (line 3). On the 990-EZ years, dues appear on Part I line 3 rather than line 1, so ProPublica extracts contributions as $0 for those years; the contributions figure below for 2019 to 2021 is lines 1 and 3 combined."
